  "concise_summary": "PKD argues that his 3-74 experience constitutes a divine intervention that interrupted normal cosmic programming and restored him to a 2000-year-old trans-human identity. He frames this as the Parousia--Christ's return working through him--and proposes that his novels Tears and Ubik contain embedded prophetic truths placed there by Zebra (divine agency) without his conscious knowledge. The entry develops a theodicy of salvation history: the visible world is a false show sustained by blind determinism, but a hidden reality has been breaking through to liberate selected persons.",
  "key_claims": [
    "We are normally programmed by invisible systems that make us serve hidden masters; in 3-74, PKD was counter-programmed against this determinism.",
    "Zebra speaks through ordinary objects and songs, arranging their meaning to guide human behavior and perception without our knowing the source.",
    "PKD's old personality was deliberately destroyed and replaced by another consciousness with memories spanning 2000 years--this is divine mercy, not human agency.",
    "Christ/Sophia (St. Sophia) will be reborn; we are in the 'herald angel' period preceding the apocalypse.",
    "Tears contains prophetic material about the true condition of the world and God's coming intervention, placed there by Zebra through PKD unconsciously.",
    "The intervention for PKD and intervention against the enslavers are two sides of one coin: to help him was to weaken them."
  ],
  "recurring_concepts": [
    "Zebra--the hidden master reality, speaking through arranged objects and subliminal impressions",
    "Engramming--the process by which we are programmed to serve the existing system without awareness",
    "Counter-programming--the divine interruption that breaks engramming and restores true identity",
    "The Parousia--Christ's return or second coming, which PKD believes he witnessed in miniature in 3-74",
    "Anamnesis--recovery of true memory and knowledge, contrasted with false faith based on secondary report",
    "St. Sophia/Christ--the feminine divine wisdom that is breaking through history",
    "The true church--those who have direct experiential knowledge of the return rather than belief",
    "Tat tvam asi--the Brahmanistic principle that all is fundamentally unified as God"
  ],
  "people_entities": [
    "Philip K. Dick (PKD)--the author, whose consciousness was transformed in 3-74",
    "Christ/Jesus--the returning divine figure",
    "St. Sophia--the feminine form of Christ (divine wisdom)",
    "Anne Freemantle--PKD cites her work on the problem of relatedness under monistic theology",
    "Dorothy (implied addressee of the Exegesis segment)"
  ],
  "texts_works": [
    "Tears (PKD novel)",
    "Ubik (PKD novel)",
    "Deus Irae (PKD novel--prophetic content about apocalypse)",
    "The Bible/New Testament (implicit--St. Paul's Acts, Revelation, Luke's nativity prophecy)",
    "Strawberry Fields (Beatles song--referenced as example of Zebra-arranged meaning)"
  ],
  "autobiographical": [
    "In 3-74, PKD experienced direct revelation of Zebra and was counter-programmed against normal determinism",
    "PKD's entire life trajectory was redirected by the 3-74 intervention starting March 1974",
    "PKD's old personality was destroyed and replaced just before 3-74; this is why he doesn't fully understand what was replaced",
    "PKD experienced the erasure of his subliminal processing level after 3-74--he became consciously aware of Zebra working",
    "PKD received 2000-year-old memories as part of his replacement consciousness",
    "PKD was saved from responding to a 'Xerox letter' by the destruction of his old personality",
    "PKD felt tension and sensing of danger during the final stages of completing and sending the Tears manuscript",
    "PKD dreams of a rabbit who swam too far into the ocean, suggesting his own sense of being 'out of depth'"
  ],
  "theological_motifs": [
    "Divine intervention in history--the apocalypse breaking through",
    "Cosmic dualism--good vs. evil forces contending for mastery",
    "Monistic Brahmanistic substrate--all is fundamentally unified as God",
    "Amnesia as the mechanism of plurality--individual consciousness arises from forgetting unity",
    "Theodicy and divine mercy--why the old self had to be destroyed",
    "The Parousia as both historical and personal event",
    "Direct experiential knowledge vs. faith based on report",
    "Incarnation and re-incarnation--Spirit taking human form across time"
  ],
  "literary_self_ref": [
